From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:25:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] migration/vmstate: skip per-field vmdesc bookkeeping when
 there is no vmdesc

Saving a VMSD without a JSON writer still paid for one on every field of
every array element: vmsd_desc_field_start() computed vmsd_can_compress()
(recursing over a struct's fields) before testing vmdesc for NULL, and
vmstate_save_field_with_vmdesc() bracketed each field with two
qemu_file_transferred() calls for a byte count only vmsd_desc_field_end()
reads, which also returns at once without a vmdesc.

qemu_save_device_state() (panda_fast_snap, COLO) passes no vmdesc. Test
vmdesc first, and read the transferred bytes only when something consumes
them. No change in behaviour on either path.

From rehosting/qemu_builder workspace/fastsnap2 (5170d14), patch 0016,
where a callgrind profile put this bookkeeping at ~19% of a device save's
instructions.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
Origin: penguin
---
 migration/vmstate.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/migration/vmstate.c b/migration/vmstate.c
index 50ebe37845285d7cc1d427d35a261dff58b914b7..4a5ed6e0452dd8b6bd9b9c8e37fba0f167443915 100644
--- a/migration/vmstate.c
+++ b/migration/vmstate.c
@@ -493,12 +493,14 @@ static void vmsd_desc_field_start(const VMStateDescription *vmsd,
 {
     char *name, *old_name;
     bool is_array = max > 1;
-    bool can_compress = vmsd_can_compress(field);
+    bool can_compress;
 
     if (!vmdesc) {
         return;
     }
 
+    can_compress = vmsd_can_compress(field);
+
     name = g_strdup(field->name);
 
     /* Field name is not unique, need to make it unique */
@@ -605,14 +607,21 @@ vmstate_save_field_with_vmdesc(QEMUFile *f, void *pv, size_t size,
                                const VMStateField *field, JSONWriter *vmdesc,
                                int i, int max, Error **errp)
 {
-    uint64_t old_offset, written_bytes;
+    uint64_t old_offset = 0, written_bytes = 0;
     bool ok;
 
     vmsd_desc_field_start(vmsd, vmdesc, field, i, max);
 
-    old_offset = qemu_file_transferred(f);
+    /* written_bytes is consumed only by vmsd_desc_field_end(), which returns
+     * immediately without a vmdesc. Without this guard both queries run for
+     * every element of every array on a path that cannot use the answer. */
+    if (vmdesc) {
+        old_offset = qemu_file_transferred(f);
+    }
     ok = vmstate_save_field(f, pv, size, field, vmdesc, errp);
-    written_bytes = qemu_file_transferred(f) - old_offset;
+    if (vmdesc) {
+        written_bytes = qemu_file_transferred(f) - old_offset;
+    }
 
     vmsd_desc_field_end(vmsd, vmdesc, field, written_bytes);
 
